What is git cherry-pick?
git cherry-pick in Git is used to copy a specific commit from one branch and apply it to another branch.
Instead of merging the whole branch, you pick only the changes you need.
Basic Syntax: git cherry-pick <commit_id>

How it works ?
You are on target branch (example: master)
Another branch (example: version1) has some commits
You pick one commit using its ID
Git applies those changes to your current branch

Example Scenario
master → main branch
version1 → feature branch
